I don't have a slackware system to check, but in a fairly standard
Solaris lashup, those manifest constants are defined in:

/usr/include/sys/errno.h

Looks like either there's a broken #include chain that should be
sucking that errno.h file into gcc when it is compiling files.c,
but is not (likely) or else slackware has changed the names for
or defining file of the error codes for file access (nearly
inconceivable, but check anyway).

An easy fix would be to locate "errno.h" in your slackware gcc
installation, and just force fit a #include for it into the top
of files.c.

